  body: "# Capital disregard: evidence and decision sequence candidate\n\n**Review state: unreviewed.
    Executable: no.**\n\n## Proposition to review\n\nThe captured guidance separates whether an item can
    be disregarded, the evidence for it and its duration. DMG 84355 places the disregard decision before
    valuation and before deemed weekly income is calculated. These are source-bound propositions, not
    findings about a claimant or an assurance of current law.\n\n## Proposed review sequence\n\n1. Identify
    the asset, relevant ownership, benefit and decision date.\n2. Identify the applicable disregard category
    and supporting evidence.\n3. Review the legal basis, amendments, commencement, territorial scope,
    DMG Memo 11/20 and any applicable decisions.\n4. Have a domain reviewer determine whether the disregard
    and period are supported; record missing or disputed evidence.\n5. Only then assess how valuation
    and deemed income should be represented for the agreed rule family.\n\nDo not infer that an unanswered
    field proves ineligibility. Do not apply the Pension Credit sequence to Universal Credit through name
    similarity.\n\n## Still required before an executable rule\n\nNamed policy and legal reviewers; the
    missing original stakeholder plan; acquired and checked provisions and memo; exceptions; effective
    dates; evidence/fraud/error requirements; review and appeal paths; synthetic positive, negative and
    boundary cases; independently accepted expected outcomes. A model-generated expected answer is not
    a gold standard.\n\nThe official instrument links identify candidate sources cited in the guidance.
    Their provisions and amendment effects have not been consolidated in this bundle.\n"
